WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.681 --> 00:00:16.426
For many days Oliver remained indoors with Fagin.

2
00:00:16.427 --> 00:00:22.339
The other boys brought home a great number of handkerchiefs, so he was kept busy picking out the monograms.

3
00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:26.077
Every morning Charley and the Dodger played their game with Fagin.

4
00:00:26.078 --> 00:00:32.331
Sometimes Oliver joined in, trying to take an item from Fagin before he felt a hand in his pocket.

5
00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:41.652
Oliver began to long for fresh air. He begged Fagin to allow him to go out to work with the others. But Fagin said he wasn't ready yet.

6
00:00:41.653 --> 00:00:47.922
Whenever the boys came home empty-handed, Fagin lectured them on the misery of idleness and lazy habits.

7
00:00:47.923 --> 00:00:53.072
Then he reinforced the importance of hard work by sending them to bed without supper.

8
00:00:53.073 --> 00:00:57.984
Seeing this, Oliver was even more anxious to be actively employed.

9
00:00:57.985 --> 00:01:06.458
For several days there were no handkerchiefs to work on. Then suddenly one morning, Fagin gave Oliver permission to go out.

10
00:01:06.459 --> 00:01:11.890
"I think today would be a good day for you to begin working, my dear," said Fagin.

11
00:01:11.891 --> 00:01:16.379
"Will I be making wallets or handkerchiefs?" Oliver asked innocently.

12
00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:21.467
Charley had another coughing fit over his coffee while the Dodger merely smiled.

13
00:01:21.468 --> 00:01:29.950
"Just follow Charley and the Dodger, and do whatever the Dodger tells you," said Fagin. "Remember, use him as your model."

14
00:01:29.951 --> 00:01:35.179
And so they went out. Oliver walked between the Dodger and Charley.

15
00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:42.366
They walked so slowly that Oliver soon began to think his companions were planning to deceive Fagin by not going to work at all.

16
00:01:42.367 --> 00:01:48.098
As they walked along, the Dodger pulled caps from the heads of small boys and tossed them out of reach.

17
00:01:48.099 --> 00:01:57.675
Charley took apples and onions from the market stalls and stuffed them into his surprisingly large pockets. This behavior looked very bad to Oliver.

18
00:01:57.676 --> 00:02:06.502
He was about to announce that he'd find his own way back to Fagin's when suddenly the Dodger stopped. He put his finger on his lip to silence the others.

19
00:02:06.503 --> 00:02:09.262
"What's the matter?" demanded Oliver.

20
00:02:09.263 --> 00:02:14.747
"Hush!" said the Dodger. "Do you see that old man outside the bookseller's?"

21
00:02:14.748 --> 00:02:19.923
"The old gentleman over there?" said Oliver. "Yes, I see him."

22
00:02:19.924 --> 00:02:22.427
"He'll do," said the Dodger.

23
00:02:22.428 --> 00:02:25.567
"A prime one," observed Charley.

24
00:02:25.568 --> 00:02:31.149
Oliver looked from one to the other with surprise, but he didn't dare ask any questions.

25
00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:36.660
Charley and the Dodger walked stealthily across the road and slunk close behind the old gentleman.

26
00:02:36.661 --> 00:02:42.807
Oliver walked a few paces after them and, not knowing what to do, looked on in silent amazement.

27
00:02:42.808 --> 00:02:49.809
The old gentleman was a very respectable-looking person with gold spectacles and an elegant bamboo cane.

28
00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:56.723
He had picked up a book from a table outside the bookseller's and there he stood, reading away as if he were sitting at home.

29
00:02:56.724 --> 00:03:05.955
He didn't appear to notice the street or the boys. Instead he stared only at the book, which he seemed to be reading with the greatest interest and eagerness.

30
00:03:05.956 --> 00:03:12.783
Suddenly, to Oliver's horror, the Dodger plunged his hand into the old man's pocket and pulled out a handkerchief.

31
00:03:12.784 --> 00:03:17.880
The Dodger handed it to Charley, and the two of them ran around the corner at full speed.

32
00:03:17.881 --> 00:03:26.011
In that instant Oliver understood the whole mystery of the handkerchiefs, the watches, the jewelry, and the "work" that the boys did for Fagin.

33
00:03:26.012 --> 00:03:30.112
He stood for a moment with the blood tingling through his veins from terror.

34
00:03:30.113 --> 00:03:37.686
He felt as if he were on fire. Then, confused and frightened, he ran away as fast as he could.

35
00:03:37.687 --> 00:03:45.764
This all happened in an instant. At the very moment when Oliver began to run, the old gentleman put his hand into his pocket.

36
00:03:45.765 --> 00:03:49.353
He discovered his handkerchief was missing and turned around.

37
00:03:49.354 --> 00:03:54.502
Seeing Oliver running away, he naturally concluded that Oliver was the thief.

38
00:03:54.503 --> 00:04:00.490
"Stop, thief!" shouted the old gentleman as he took off after Oliver with the book still in his hand.

39
00:04:00.491 --> 00:04:04.070
The old gentleman was not the only one who cried out.

40
00:04:04.071 --> 00:04:09.397
Charley and the Dodger had not wanted to attract attention by running down the open street.

41
00:04:09.398 --> 00:04:12.898
They had merely hidden in the first doorway around the corner.

42
00:04:12.899 --> 00:04:18.754
As soon as they saw Oliver running and heard the old gentleman shouting, they knew what had happened.

43
00:04:18.755 --> 00:04:22.908
"Stop, thief!" they shouted as they joined in the pursuit.

44
00:04:22.909 --> 00:04:32.229
This upset Oliver even more. So away he went like the wind with the old gentleman and the two boys roaring and shouting behind him.

45
00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:40.626
Hearing the commotion, the baker threw down his basket. The milkman left his pail. The errand boy abandoned his parcels.

46
00:04:40.627 --> 00:04:46.870
The tradesman left his counter. Away they all ran after Oliver, with everyone shouting.

47
00:04:46.871 --> 00:04:54.118
"Stop, thief! Stop, thief!" The cry was taken up by what seemed like a hundred voices.

48
00:04:54.119 --> 00:04:58.184
At last a man caught up to Oliver and dragged him to the ground.

49
00:04:58.185 --> 00:05:01.376
"Give the boy some air!" cried the baker.

50
00:05:01.377 --> 00:05:05.018
"Nonsense! He doesn't deserve it!" said the milkman.

51
00:05:05.019 --> 00:05:08.519
"Here comes the old man!" said the errand boy.

52
00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:11.610
"Is this the boy, sir?" asked the tradesman.

53
00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:16.601
Covered with mud and bleeding from his lip, Oliver lay on the ground.

54
00:05:16.602 --> 00:05:21.927
He looked wildly at the faces surrounding him while the old gentleman was dragged into the circle.

55
00:05:21.928 --> 00:05:27.747
"Yes," said the old gentleman, looking Oliver in the eye. "I am afraid it is the boy."

56
00:05:27.748 --> 00:05:32.245
"Afraid!" murmured the crowd. "That's a good one!"

57
00:05:32.246 --> 00:05:36.319
"Poor fellow, he has hurt himself," said the old gentleman.

58
00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:42.908
"I did that, sir, and I cut my knuckle against his teeth," said a burly fellow. "I stopped him, sir."

59
00:05:42.909 --> 00:05:47.307
He touched his hat with a grin, expecting some reward for his pains.

60
00:05:47.308 --> 00:05:51.161
But the old gentleman eyed him with an expression of dislike.

61
00:05:51.162 --> 00:05:54.810
The old gentleman looked as if he wanted to run away too.

62
00:05:54.811 --> 00:06:00.312
But at that moment a police officer made his way through the crowd and seized Oliver by the collar.

63
00:06:00.313 --> 00:06:04.298
"Come on, get up," the policeman said roughly.

64
00:06:04.299 --> 00:06:12.208
"It wasn't me, sir. Indeed it was two other boys," said Oliver, looking around. "They're here somewhere."

65
00:06:12.209 --> 00:06:15.126
"Oh, no, they aren't," said the policeman.

66
00:06:15.127 --> 00:06:20.884
And he was right, because Charley and the Dodger had disappeared down the first alley they'd come to.

67
00:06:20.885 --> 00:06:23.636
"Get up," said the policeman again.

68
00:06:23.637 --> 00:06:27.128
"Don't hurt him," said the old gentleman with concern.

69
00:06:27.129 --> 00:06:34.200
"Oh, I wouldn't think of hurting him," said the policeman sarcastically. "Will you stand upon your legs, you young devil?"

70
00:06:34.201 --> 00:06:38.539
Oliver did not reply, but instead tried to rise to his feet.

71
00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:43.696
The policeman grabbed Oliver's jacket collar and dragged him down the street at a rapid pace.

72
00:06:43.697 --> 00:06:50.152
The old gentleman walked by the policeman's side, and the crowd followed along behind.
